  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.7: Quantinuum and Atom Computing Backends, QRNG, Async Improvements, Enhanced Quantum Chemistry\n- NEW: Quantinuum Backend (H1, H2 series) with dynamic qubit limits and improved gate support (S, T, SDG, TDG)\n- NEW: Atom Computing Phoenix Backend (100+ qubit neutral atom quantum computer) with gate support\n- NEW: Quantum Random Number Generation (QRNG) with true quantum randomness, multi-bit generation, statistical validation\n- NEW: Async execution methods for quantum solvers (ExecuteAsync pattern) and algorithm adapters\n- IMPROVED: Quantum Chemistry - Enhanced fermion mappings (Jordan-Wigner, Bravyi-Kitaev, Parity), molecular Hamiltonians\n- IMPROVED: Backend capability detection for Quantinuum and Atom Computing platforms\n- IMPROVED: Circuit builder with extended gate transpilation for new backends\n- IMPROVED: Model serialization and data preprocessing for ML algorithms\n- IMPROVED: Progress reporting with cancellation support for AutoML workflows\n- IMPROVED: Batch accumulator with better async handling\n- ADDED: Comprehensive hardware selection guide and mathematical foundations documentation\n- ADDED: Examples for QRNG, cancellation/progress monitoring, topological computing\n- Status: 1400+ tests passing in main package, production-ready",
